       "PRINCIPLE_NUMBER_LINE",
       "PRINCIPLE_MULTIPLE_REPRESENTATIONS",
       "PRINCIPLE_WORKED_EXAMPLE"
      ],
      "rationale": "Lining up two number lines makes equivalence a fact about position, before any rule about multiplying the numerator and denominator. The second line cuts each part into 2 or 3, so the rule later explains something students have seen.",
